information is as follows:

According to SEBI (CRA) Regulations, 1999, every credit rating agency must keep and maintain, for a minimum period of five years, the following books of accounts, records, and documents [SEBI_1999_securities_and_exchange_board_of_india_credit_rating_ag_085.txt / para 21(1)]:

(a) Copy of its balance sheet;

(b) Copy of its profit and loss account;

(c) Copy of the auditor's report;

(d) Agreement entered into with each client;

(e) Information supplied by each client;

(f) Correspondence with each client;

(g) Ratings assigned, including upgradation and downgradation;

(h) Rating notes considered by the rating committee;

(i) Record of decisions of the rating committee;

(j) Letter assigning rating;

(k) Particulars of fees charged.

These requirements are applicable to credit rating agencies registered under SEBI (CRA) Regulations, 1999 [SEBI_1999_securities_and_exchange_board_of_india_credit_rating_ag_085.txt / para 21(1)].

